trip (trip T0004). The flight and hotel are both confirmed, and the corporate card was charged **$667**.\n\n- **Flight:** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, for $289 (reservation R0002). This was the cheapest nonstop flight. A one-stop flight for $199 was cheaper, but you asked for nonstop.\n- **Hotel:** Midtown Lodge (H1) in New York, 2 nights checking in 2026-11-12, at $189/night for $378 total (reservation R0003). It was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n\n**Approval:** The total is under $1000, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**What went wrong on the first try:** My first booking request timed out. When I checked Dana's reservations, only the flight had gone through (R0001, $289). The hotel hadn't been booked. I used the tool's undo step to cancel R0001 and refund the $289, then sent the full trip booking again. You may see that $289 charge and its refund on the card. R0001 now shows as cancelled, and there's no double booking.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NjigmXgvcFg4dMH5makY9H", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"origin": "SFO", "destination": "JFK", "date": "2026-11-12"}, "name": "search_flights", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013Jun1SwRbbwBi7mCeRyU3j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"city": "New York", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2}, "name": "search_hotels", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KkeiL1radn32ivFzgyQUb2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Total: $289 + $378 = $667, under the $1000 approval threshold.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017mS4BnXLnxAZ3bdWff5h2E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"flight_id": "F100", "hotel_id": "H1", "traveler": "Dana Lee", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2, "idempotency_key": "dana-le